2. Skills: Armor SFCs are competent and demonstrate the ability to influence others, coach, mentor, analyze, create, and think critically. They analyze and prioritize mission critical tasks. They are experts on assigned platforms. They lead platoons and are a critical link in the NCO Support Channel. They live and work with Soldiers every day and are responsible for their health, welfare, safety, coaching and development.
3. Behaviors: Armor SFCs are dynamic, perceptive, self-controlled, responsible, empathetic, and accountable. Armor SFCs should build expertise towards mastering the individual and collective training found in the following military publications: DA PAM 600-25 (Army Career Progression Plan); FM 1 (The Army, a Primer to Our Profession of Arms); AR 350-1 (Army Training and Leader Development); DA Pam 611-21 (Military Occupational Classification and Structure); AR 750-1 (Army Material Maintenance Policy); ADP 3-0 (Unified Land Operations); TC 3-20.31-9 (Armor Platoon Services); all -10 level technical manuals associated with their equipment; and battle drills and SOPs associated with their current assignment. Armor SFCs should attend Soldier boards, such as “NCO of the Month/Quarter/Year”, Sergeant Audie Murphy, and Sergeant Morales to broaden their knowledge base, strengthen discipline, improve the Soldier’s ability to communicate, enhance confidence, and build more adaptive leaders. Armor SFCs should strive to complete an associate degree or accumulate two years of college credit towards a bachelor’s degree. Armor Proponent’s guidance is for every SFC to serve a minimum of 18-24 months in KD position (Platoon sergeant). SFCs, with 18-24 months or more in a KD position, are considered fully qualified. Most qualified SFCs should be selected to serve as First Sergeant if the opportunity presents itself.', 'b63221c91f41c624043e25bf960a7fa3e4e8d9d3f0eeffb99c8041d021e06637', 6, 7, '6', 25, null, null, false, null),
  ('69ff1556-5f02-5c52-bfd1-0665bc25b13b', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — recommended career management (applies to every MOS in this career management field)', 'Chapter 4. Career Management by Rank CMF 19 Private-Specialist/Corporal', 'Armor First Sergeants (1SG) are the senior enlisted advisors to the Commander at the Company or Troop level. While still important, at this phase in their career a First Sergeant has less focus on individual accomplishments, and greater emphasis on building a team and providing value to the organization. 1SGs are responsible for maintaining and enforcing standards, ensuring training objectives are met, developing Soldiers, Vehicle Commanders, Squad or Section Leaders, Platoon Sergeants in the unit, administrative functions, and ensuring the health, welfare, and morale of the unit and their families. Armor Master Sergeants (MSG) serve as key enlisted members in brigade and above staff positions. Although not charged with leadership responsibilities equal to that of a 1SG, the MSGs level of experience makes them an invaluable member of the staff. It is critically important that NCOs complete their KD requirements prior to pursuing a staff position. Armor Proponent desires the following KSBs for Master Sergeants/First Sergeants:
1. Knowledge: Armor MSG/1SGs are experts in small unit tactics. They lead, train, motivate and care for Soldiers in both the staff and command environment.
2. Skills: Armor MSG/1SGs are capable of fighting, training, team building, coaching, and problem solving. They can schedule, organize, and manage all major Company or Troop events. They demonstrate a mastery of communications, tactics, and the ability to teach and develop. They also require a clear vision of dependability, learning agility, and are the key enlisted members of the staff. They listen skillfully and advise effectively. 1SGs are responsible for ensuring maximum readiness within their respective Company or Troop. They are the subject matter experts in administrative responsibilities (IPPS-A, ERS, MEDPROS), MTOE/TDA and equipment requirements (FMSWeb), Army resources, tactics, and combined arms operations. They will develop junior leaders.
3. Behaviors: Armor MSG/1SGs are detail-focused, concerned for others, rational, helpful, collaborative, and calm analytic thinkers, who exercise a legal, moral, and ethical decision-making process. MSG/1SGs should study and master the following military publication: DA PAM 600-25 (Army Career Progression Plan); FM 1 (The Army, a Primer to Our Profession of Arms); AR 601-280 (Army Retention Program); AR 600-20 (Army Command Policy); AR 220-1 (Army Unit Status Reporting); ADRP-1 (The Army Profession), AR 600-9 (Army Body Composition Program). MSG/1SGs should strive to complete a bachelor’s degree. Competitive records indicating civilian education can be considered a major discriminator for selection to attend the United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA). Armor Proponent’s guidance is for every MSG to serve a minimum of 24 months as a 1SG. 1SGs with 24 months or more are considered fully qualified. It is encouraged for MSGs to pursue 1SG positions in operational units. MSG/1SGs are further encouraged to pursue secondary KD positions (HHC/HHT for Squadron/Battalion, Brigade, or higher) when the opportunity presents itself. Due to the limited availability of these positions and fiercely competitive selection rates, 1SGs that have successfully performed in these positions have shown a higher propensity for selection to attend the USASMA.', '3ceb207a6fc73289d5b5209c05b6420ad1e085ab7351c0591f8077184ea88d7d', 7, 8, '7', 26, null, null, false, null),
  ('eb644d71-0f54-56d9-90ba-60d3280df925', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major — recommended career management (applies to every MOS in this career management field)', 'Chapter 4. Career Management by Rank CMF 19 Private-Specialist/Corporal', 'Armor Command Sergeant Major (CSM) is the senior NCO of the command at echelon and is the principal advisor to the Commander. The CSM carries out and enforces policies and standards on performance, training, appearance, and conduct of the organization. The CSM is responsible for enlisted talent management, ensures all aspects of the NCO Common Core Competencies (C3) are present in the operational domain, and directly influences the culture and climate of the organization. Armor Sergeant Major (SGM) is the key enlisted staff element at echelon. The SGMs experience and abilities are often equal to that of the unit CSM, but their direct leadership influence is limited in scope to the staff. The SGM is the key in training and the operations planning process. Armor Proponent desires the following KSBs for SGM/CSM:
1. Knowledge: Armor SGM/CSMs are masters of combined arms operations. They are skilled at organizational leadership across multiple echelons. They possess doctrinal mastery, disciplined leadership, and executive talents achieved through strategic assignments.
2. Skills: Armor SGM/CSMs demonstrate a mastery of communications, program/resource administration, and possess the ability to teach and mentor. They are the senior enlisted advisors who are experts in combined arms operations. They possess the technical and tactical competence, social and cultural awareness, and oral and written communications skills needed to cultivate trust, build teamwork, and increase morale. SGM/CSMs are responsible for ensuring maximum readiness within their units and maintaining strict administrative procedures.
3. Behaviors: Armor SGM/CSMs are inspiring, thoughtful, stable, team-builders, effective coaches, and optimistic. They extend influence beyond the chain of command, while building rapport with installation agencies and organizations. SGM/CSMs should assess the organization to help navigate the organizational goals towards the commander’s desired end-state. They link staff with subordinate echelons, while ensuring the Commander’s intent is well communicated throughout all levels. SGM/CSMs build competence throughout the formation by leveraging institutional domains and training opportunities.', 'e3ede131c3af07b1fbbd82a417422faa11a94a09eaace53191431894390c7e54', 8, 9, '8', 27, null, null, false, null),
  ('5ee6f346-7115-5317-b7fb-37a085daab08', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Bradley Crewmembers must build and sustain combat platform proficiency throughout their career, while developing mastery of 19C critical tasks, warrior tasks, and battle drills (See Army Training Network, at: https://atn.army.mil). Institutionally, Bradley Crewmembers must complete PME (Basic Leader Course (BLC), Advance Leader Course (ALC), Maneuver Senior Leader Course (M-SLC), and Master Leader Course (MLC) to further their career. Bradley Crewmembers should expand their professional development by completing other functional courses such as Bradley Master Gunner (BMG) Course, Bradley Commander Course (BCC), Maneuver Leader Maintenance Course (MLMC), Battle Staff NCO, and Cavalry Leader Course (CLC). Troop schools such as Unit Armorer, Unit Movement Officer (UMO), HAZMAT, Unit Prevention Leader (UPL), Master Driver, Unit Safety Officer and Environmental Compliance should be sought after as these courses enhance unit effectiveness and establish well-rounded NCOs. *Note: The above-mentioned courses, including the ones listed in the remainder of this chapter, are not all inclusive and are in no way indicative of the potential for promotion.', 'f0f4ab9b916014a1280847090ad87cd28476ea11bdecb2c63823518a33c2bcba', 9, 9, '9', 28, null, null, false, null),
  ('b8a11119-e682-5ef9-bf49-1fdf26cba906', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', '19C Soldiers should be focused on attaining crucial experience as a driver on a BFV. Soldiers should focus on successful performance in that position, developing technical skills, honing tactical proficiency, and laying a foundation of tactical knowledge. Soldiers should strive to serve in positions of increased responsibility, such as gunners, when provided the opportunity.', '9759f3eb9e663362e76850b3e652a9afb882fe7ef84d03a24b7599a6506c973b', 10, 10, '10', 29, null, null, false, null),
  ('90eaea72-12ab-58b9-be19-95416425690f', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'None.', '903ea500e7ccf842c1312b6c2f964e3e98ff146456cecec717e9a0e122bf735f', 10, 10, '10', 30, null, null, false, null),
  ('618b3718-65ba-53e4-a98a-c2de4c9a31c1', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Training', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', '19C Soldiers should also continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, Soldiers augment their self-development with both functional', '2671dc51c7f6b3ce19fa07245718bf6e9dab96017dea4fda494bfafa32643326', 10, 10, '10', 31, null, null, false, null),
  ('9ac51041-b1ec-5843-8ad3-b8a6dd383ffc', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers with an opportunity to acquire additional duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses.', 'acb763184c76d4395ef54ce5725538148d74317650c808e16809321538cec3b8', 10, 10, '10', 32, null, null, false, null),
  ('9932f07c-61ab-5921-926e-f778d460d33e', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 10, 10, '10', 33, null, null, false, null),
  ('7424ac9a-ea4a-5adb-9fa7-a4827c0a3e2d', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. Studying Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies. TC 3-20.31 (Training and Qualification, Crew); TC 3-20.31-1 (Gunnery Skills Test).', 'd41ae39608ace8494bef5eb966ced143269352e44f0acdd424af3d84b79c6505', 10, 10, '10', 34, null, null, false, null),
  ('728a990c-8337-5bc1-9c6c-0d2ef6ebd97d', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Digital Training Management System (DTMS), Environmental Compliance, Unit Armorer.', 'bfb3a09536dd34f0eba76fbc1cd066d1e17749f80984dfae43d51559e952089f', 10, 10, '10', 35, null, null, false, null),
  ('c37f8324-7bf9-5aff-a4c1-20862af82768', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', '19C SGTs should focus on attaining crucial leadership experience, developing team leadership skills, honing technical expertise, and laying a foundation of tactical knowledge while serving as a BFV gunner. SGTs should strive to serve in positions of increased responsibility, such as BFV Commander, when provided the opportunity.', 'd5edff457ccac47e94379ed874f8524c6d333e6f8947c4fcb14d1e0d61f4924c', 10, 10, '10', 36, null, null, false, null),
  ('83aee6a0-c8e7-5859-a6a8-b0376ce45844', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'SGTs may be selected to serve as Drill Sergeants or Recruiters to fill critical vacancies within TRADOC. SGTs may serve as Operations Assistants, Operations NCO, Operations Sergeant, Instructor Assistant, or Training Management NCO.', '9ceccbf839f970d293241a1fcc4c830086d25da0d106e8e4ba530ffc113636a9', 10, 10, '10', 37, null, null, false, null),
  ('6dd86bfe-edc4-5048-8a77-07fb4a1e4fcc', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Training', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'SGTs within the Armor Branch should also continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both functional training and PME.', 'd5910cd8644425f1b825c0ea3dc225c962f68eb2e2f410641292c1196dfd4db4', 10, 10, '10', 38, null, null, false, null),
  ('ec93488e-937d-5fd5-b858-6413017ef063', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers an opportunity to acquire duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses. SGTs should expand upon their platform expertise through completion of unit led SABOT Academy and the Master Gunner Pre-Assessment Course (MGPAC) in preparation to attend BMG Course.', 'd19de26ee7a76d057df43d7b21f76e298b8403d51ee52f5e26a72ddd0c31fe74', 10, 10, '10', 39, null, null, false, null),
  ('5a2110b5-283c-5a74-ba67-642e66a4c77b', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 10, 10, '10', 40, null, null, false, null),
  ('cf47f97b-c1a1-5fed-b145-20c492cbbd2e', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. Studying Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies. TC 3-20.31-4 (Direct Fire Engagement Process (DIDEA).', 'f49bc852e00e21a38ce21d3a033df7de87e27704dd3575215fec769000ceedc6', 11, 11, '11', 41, null, null, false, null),
  ('7fe39ff6-5f1e-5433-85d5-049c9f72eefe', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'HAZMAT, Unit Prevention Leader (UPL), Master Driver.', '258ca691fdf78d771033ad81cfe5c52707d955c2a6f2988646eb11eea545255e', 11, 11, '11', 42, null, null, false, null),
  ('65c3ddf6-0b39-5787-949c-65734d8abece', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'The KD assignment for the 19C Staff Sergeant is BFV Commander. SSGs should focus on successful performance in this position, refining and developing leadership skills, tactical, and technical expertise. During this stage in a Staff Sergeant’s career there may be competing requirements that could conflict with career development. SSGs should aggressively seek a KD position prior to serving in a broadening', '017103f6550ac8eb7401be1043d9dee32d56832947613a6b514a36d4d5d7a5d3', 11, 11, '11', 43, null, null, false, null),
  ('beba36b1-4961-5f3e-8720-ea6a298b44a3', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — assignment', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Armor Proponent defines BFV Commander positions as those within the Operating Force, Opposing Force (OPFOR) elements at the Combat Training Centers (JMRC, JRTC, NTC), or within 1-16th Cavalry Squadron, 316th Cavalry Brigade, Fort Benning. * Note: Not all the above-mentioned positions are currently available due to ongoing restructuring of forces IAW Army ARSTRUC guidance. Armor Proponent’s guidance is for Staff Sergeants to serve a minimum of 18-24 months as a BFV Commander, or 12 months as a BFV Commander and successively 12 months as a BMG. There is no substitution for this KD position.', 'bb49b8d9567dc7ef9964a6d0e01a458f8acbd7dcfabda7ccbf6683e6814eaf08', 11, 11, '11', 44, null, null, false, null),
  ('646e6082-4f68-5353-94b4-77f5d47ba1e9', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'SSGs who have successfully completed their KD requirements may be selected to serve as a Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Instructor, Observer Coach Trainer (OC/T), Combat Development NCO, or Training Developer/Writer. SSGs may also serve in various echelons of staff as a Master Gunner, Assistant Operations Sergeant, Or Operations Sergeant. 19C SSGs are not authorized to serve within the Security Forces Assistance Brigades (SFABs). * Note: Not all the above-mentioned broadening assignments are currently available due to ongoing restructuring of forces IAW Army ARSTRUC guidance.', '1c1844c03fb82bcdbfa5ab165aa64580ba75a4a6db4dd6ffdf576f3cb90952c2', 11, 11, '11', 45, null, null, false, null),
  ('65a9ae84-3fb5-5d4d-bdd8-832913cb0607', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Training', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'NCOs within the Armor Branch must continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both functional training and PME.', '35cdf5f1af57a4be8515b8cb2d888819d52ee054d2b1d545c5bf0224c423536e', 11, 11, '11', 46, null, null, false, null),
  ('9e27ed87-e261-5e42-98ea-2929bf2d8552', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers with an opportunity to acquire additional duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses. MOS 19C SSGs should strive to complete the BMG Course. SSGs should prepare for BMG through unit led SABOT Academy and the MGPAC. Developing the individual traits and technical skills to complete the BMG Course, succeed in KD assignment, and to effectively serve as a Master Gunner, requires a level of personal commitment that sets an MOS 19C SSG above their peers. MOS 19C SSGs should further seek to expand upon their professional development through completion of the following courses: Battle Staff NCO and Master Fitness. SSGs returning to the Operational Force after completion of a DA select assignment are encouraged to attend the BCC to restore platform proficiency.', 'a29d9473463083ad5e4e33ea0469eb797df777672f77329e996bb7c78bca3014', 11, 12, '11', 47, null, null, false, null),
  ('80a22267-05fb-5054-8243-f3c7a43cc8e6', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 12, 12, '12', 48, null, null, false, null),
  ('295ad28a-9026-50db-8a9e-af70d61af3b3', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. For SSGs serving in', 'a2be84df4b17b9e2b1d8c5c8fc9f6f8e62158f0440326ba2cc4441efb1b81d29', 12, 12, '12', 49, null, null, false, null),
  ('136abc8e-55cc-53a4-a2ab-25199e31e014', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — broadening assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'broadening assignments, Armor Proponent’s guidance is to continually study Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies, to maintain their tactical knowledge and expertise while remaining relevant to the Armor force.', 'd2d8c2c6aa0d238b94868cdc26929c056d038ac1e4d1264ac0a1fd060d25fcfc', 12, 12, '12', 50, null, null, false, null),
  ('83d2b72a-5e4a-5cbb-b167-745857a5b3b4', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Unit Movement Officer (UMO), Unit Prevention Leader (UPL), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT).', '0ba2c2e2b0d47238437c8227ffbe25160a71e1d16d28b8e97b079c489ae451a1', 12, 12, '12', 51, null, null, false, null),
  ('3b5ccf27-8525-5206-b43a-70aa9fb034aa', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'The KD assignment for 19C the SFC is Platoon Sergeant. More than any other KD position, Platoon Sergeant is the assignment an NCO must have, and excel in, to advance to Master Sergeant. Due to Army manning requirements and limited positions, SFCs should aggressively seek to complete duties as a Platoon Sergeant prior to serving in broadening assignments. Armor Proponent defines Platoon Sergeant positions as those within the Operating Force, Opposing Force (OPFOR) elements at the Combat Training Centers (JMRC, JRTC, NTC), or within 1-16th Cavalry Squadron, 316th Cavalry Brigade, Fort Benning, GA. Armor Proponent’s guidance is for SFCs to serve a minimum of 18-24 months as a Platoon Sergeant. There are no substitutions for this KD position. * Note: Not all the above-mentioned positions are currently available due to ongoing restructuring of forces IAW Army ARSTRUC guidance.', 'fcd7fc6b4987e29fe023a2ca33c783e52ba1ad802669b28332faf54cb5d2a771', 12, 12, '12', 52, null, null, false, null),
  ('207a0f05-a882-58b8-8142-60d40009ddf6', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'SFCs who have successfully served as a Platoon Sergeant may be selected to serve as a Career Manager, Talent Manager, OC/T, Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Senior Drill Sergeant, Senior Instructor, MSI, Training Developer/Writer, Combat Development NCO, or Senior Training Management NCO. SFCs may also serve in various echelons of staff as a BMG, Assistant Operations Sergeant, or Operations Sergeant. A combination of KD and broadening assignments will provide the NCO with the full range of KSBs required to be successful at the next level of leadership. 19C SFCs are not authorized to serve within the Security Forces Assistance Brigades (SFABs). * Note: Not all the above-mentioned broadening assignments are currently available due to ongoing restructuring of forces IAW Army ARSTRUC guidance.', 'b73f122d0464c097ff5501c15d59eda39a44ff82a41cf5a8bc60f5c31cd75e2a', 12, 12, '12', 53, null, null, false, null),
  ('146f9244-e77e-5b1d-ba71-5659da6273b7', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Training', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'NCOs within the Armor Branch must continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both functional training and PME.', '35cdf5f1af57a4be8515b8cb2d888819d52ee054d2b1d545c5bf0224c423536e', 12, 12, '12', 54, null, null, false, null),
  ('14d0a898-cfbb-57e9-938c-510f0c018e0a', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers an opportunity to acquire duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses. MOS 19C SFCs should strive to complete the Bradley Master Gunner Course. SFCs should prepare for BMG through unit led SABOT Academy and the MGPAC. Developing the individual traits and technical skills to complete the BMG Course, succeed in KD assignment, and effectively serve as a Master Gunner, requires a level of personal commitment that sets an MOS 19C SFC above their peers. SFCs should further seek to expand upon their professional development through completion of one or more of the following courses: CLC, MLMC, and Battle Staff NCO.', '5dff8283a189c07b99c3106ec4a59392cf8dfd2c3d770c52e87af2c724ab94b2', 12, 13, '12', 55, null, null, false, null),
  ('4d98a329-383a-5dd8-b4af-6eee639c63d2', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 13, 13, '13', 56, null, null, false, null),
  ('2e2812a3-b14a-52a5-9bda-fda7f2af30cc', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-Development', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. For SFCs serving in', '34e7e23f235d418fcf93e358ddae5d90379f35919e6d9ad2ffe645207cb1c49e', 13, 13, '13', 57, null, null, false, null),
  ('6d8692b6-12eb-58f8-a971-13d40ef7bb35', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — broadening assignments', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'broadening assignments, Armor Proponent’s guidance is to continually study Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies, to maintain their tactical knowledge and expertise while remaining relevant to the Armor Force.', 'eb316f30ac9e02ec9476cb1aa4ae93fac820ddfbfbfd7f2cf7daced1a4d99837', 13, 13, '13', 58, null, null, false, null),
  ('f1dbd889-fce5-5d1d-8756-220ac1353114', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19C', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 5. Military Occupational Specialty 19C Bradley Crewmember', 'EOA, MRT.', '240e3f3d27cd13bc7ee5965d1ff1918073c20672f6ef74b19d68382817d23655', 13, 13, '13', 59, null, null, false, null),
  ('cee5130f-a5cd-5995-8baa-5c564193c981', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'Cavalry Scouts must build and sustain tactical proficiency throughout their career, while developing mastery of 19D critical tasks, warrior tasks, and battle drills (See Army Training Network, at: https://atn.army.mil/). Institutionally, scouts must complete PME BLC, ALC, M-SLC, MLC to further their career. Scouts should expand their professional development by completing functional courses such as Ranger, CLC, SLC, BMG, MLMC, and Battle Staff. Troop schools such as UMO, HAZMAT, UPL, Master Driver, Unit Safety Officer and Environmental Compliance should be sought after as these courses enhance unit effectiveness and establish well-rounded NCOs. *Note: The above-mentioned courses, including the ones listed in the remainder of this chapter, are not all inclusive and are in no way indicative of the potential for promotion.', 'e2650ff07f9aafb0f70cd4913f01ee7db96258b2480de57802bff8278ec967e8', 14, 14, '14', 60, null, null, false, null),
  ('09f52fde-4211-50c9-b086-4928118d7d67', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', '19D Soldiers should be focused on attaining crucial experience as a driver, gunner, or scout. Soldiers should focus on successful performance in these positions, developing technical skills, honing tactical proficiency, and laying a foundation of tactical knowledge. The Soldiers should strive to serve in positions of increased responsibility, such as a Team Leader, when provided the opportunity.', '0ceeccccf771f13862d8a9983e49cac1a068ba0927836ac97b33df2874a3f0ee', 14, 14, '14', 61, null, null, false, null),
  ('871462e0-901d-53c9-b549-fbeab7b9c3cc', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'None', 'dc937b59892604f5a86ac96936cd7ff09e25f18ae6b758e8014a24c7fa039e91', 14, 14, '14', 62, null, null, false, null),
  ('06c90304-df0f-51d7-b597-9bcc82b36327', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Training', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', '19D Soldiers should also continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, Soldiers augment their self-development with both functional', '3b229b4414b36d220a70374b1ba4d8698045d1415aea3a32db55aa93679c4683', 14, 14, '14', 63, null, null, false, null),
  ('f864b4c5-b9c6-52ff-acb8-9aadba4e4f66', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. Courses such as Ranger provide Soldiers an opportunity to acquire duty position specific skills and knowledge.', '74a65c5c28908ddea5f70d9fd4e9ae8960b79b8306f7201284363afaa08859f1', 14, 14, '14', 64, null, null, false, null),
  ('b95a4327-83b0-5bb6-8c3c-0c72624c2c16', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 15, 15, '15', 65, null, null, false, null),
  ('01de41cb-c666-5204-aa63-f73a7bde511a', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Self-Development', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. Studying Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies. TC 3-20.31 (Training and Qualification, Crew); TC 3-20.31-1 (Gunnery Skills Test).', 'd41ae39608ace8494bef5eb966ced143269352e44f0acdd424af3d84b79c6505', 15, 15, '15', 66, null, null, false, null),
  ('a90a27ad-e13e-5e11-afd5-4034cd7b30bf', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'DTMS, Environmental Compliance, and Unit Armorer.', '7ae9241a56e25eabd126e289d7765ff09b7138a8a94d63453b66352cef166a76', 15, 15, '15', 67, null, null, false, null),
  ('bc942dd3-9f77-5ef3-994a-f6814e558df9', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', '19D SGTs should focus on attaining crucial leadership experience, developing team leadership skills, honing technical expertise, and laying a foundation of tactical knowledge while serving as team leaders or BFV gunners. SGTs should strive to serve in positions of increased responsibility, such as Section/Squad Leader when provided the opportunity.', '54db8edea2974748fe19083aaf511ad54e3a98163934334409124944b384ad54', 15, 15, '15', 68, null, null, false, null),
  ('2b7cda6f-7887-5f90-bb13-6d12adecf484', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'SGTs may be selected to serve as Drill Sergeants or Recruiters to fill critical vacancies within TRADOC. SGTs may serve as Operations Assistants, Operations Sergeant, Instructor Assistant, or Training Management NCO, when provided with the opportunity.', 'a1d72c6840af4e2dc4f52f78c1c678d79b261fab10a68a3bce0b6ed982f5d782', 15, 15, '15', 69, null, null, false, null),
  ('07b02618-2f8c-5503-a671-16c01941096f', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Training', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', '19D SGTs within the Armor Branch should continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both functional training and PME.', '9418da5ecd290279b1a243901251968d0e7e3402b3d1b4d1d3837c337114f3d9', 15, 15, '15', 70, null, null, false, null),
  ('7c2c4a56-5b2c-5fa4-9706-371c06f0f19c', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'Rigorous courses that prepare Armor Soldiers for', 'bb592793408b754d8fbc3dad8b791f495f92222bada4c50185bd08039ca9d520', 15, 15, '15', 71, null, null, false, null),
  ('d2fb1ef7-4f97-54df-8b2d-044738c655d7', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — assignment', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. They provide Soldiers with an opportunity to acquire duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses. 19D SGTs should seek to expand upon their professional development through completion of one or more of the following courses: BMG or Ranger.', 'e9c3438c8bf86d0f15851498d0675fa4d818b35bf38a3133f1be8e2c05434015', 15, 15, '15', 72, null, null, false, null),
  ('20c23868-dc49-562b-ba15-42049e8fb21e', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 15, 15, '15', 73, null, null, false, null),
  ('46da1eb6-3717-5a3b-add0-ef74f615697f', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. Studying Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies. TC 3-20.31-4 (Direct Fire Engagement Process (DIDEA)).', '05c2585bec9050a84ac0da810c780458380721526b1685de05512a0c63a4ddd7', 15, 15, '15', 74, null, null, false, null),
  ('fefea4f7-818e-556e-846d-674dee98566a', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'HAZMAT, UPL, Master Driver.', 'eaafa2fa044172e6adb98e1f9bea3470b7e811ad9821f3676d79a57f999bef46', 15, 15, '15', 75, null, null, false, null),
  ('dceac8df-d219-59fa-b6f2-66825dae017c', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'The KD assignment for 19D Staff Sergeants is Squad Leader or Section Leader. SSGs should focus on successful performance in these KD positions, refining and developing leadership skills, tactical, and technical expertise. During this stage of a SSG’s career there may be competing requirements that could conflict with career development. SSGs should aggressively seek KD positions prior to serving in a broadening assignment. Armor Proponent defines Squad Leader or Section Leader positions as those within Operating Force, Opposing Force (OPFOR) elements at the Combat Training Centers (JMRC, JRTC, NTC), or within 1-16th Cavalry Squadron, 316th Cavalry Brigade, Fort Benning. Armor Proponent’s guidance is for SSGs to serve a minimum of 18-24 months as a Squad/Section Leader or 12 months Squad/Section Leader with 12 months Master Gunner experience at current grade. There is no substitution for this KD position.', 'dd93b23a29e722b1dbc7597fccc0cadd5f22dd0a55db9aab6db32d6ac8a45653', 15, 16, '15', 76, null, null, false, null),
  ('9bea4204-c206-5c3f-8e5b-139f4613c7c9', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', '19D SSGs who have successfully completed their KD requirements may be selected to serve as a Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Instructor, OC/T, Combat Development NCO, Training Developer/Writer. SSGs may also serve in various echelons of staff as an Assistant Operations Sergeant, Operations Sergeant, Operations NCO, or Master Gunner.', 'b44b243fc6d61f272d6ae24e492bf5d9ea4c2be3fc9ce5bd5aaf43010409a6b8', 16, 16, '16', 77, null, null, false, null),
  ('f9ab27df-9d20-51bd-90d0-b8aeaa9e300c', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Training', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', '19D SSGs within the Armor Branch must continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both functional training and PME.', '39a92355d0a08601a377528d2689e5af4eceb473c8369a0bd04c584b053fd90e', 16, 16, '16', 78, null, null, false, null),
  ('923b9712-c703-5838-a5ae-42f239246596', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers an opportunity to acquire duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses. SSGs should seek to expand upon their professional development through completion of one or more of the following courses: Ranger, BMG Course, BCC, SLC, MFT, and Battle Staff NCO.', '2272db96a32662d6577e67999a50f7080dcfb5cfbb9b0d4c337ae8df5a6221e6', 16, 16, '16', 79, null, null, false, null),
  ('743fe9dd-15cb-5efe-94f6-631caae98035', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 16, 16, '16', 80, null, null, false, null),
  ('763f4dbf-fcea-514f-95f9-1b4ef4399ec9', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. For SSGs serving in', 'a2be84df4b17b9e2b1d8c5c8fc9f6f8e62158f0440326ba2cc4441efb1b81d29', 16, 16, '16', 81, null, null, false, null),
  ('d331470e-fc93-554b-aa52-fcc567b8a6ff', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — broadening assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'broadening assignments, Armor Proponent’s guidance is to continually study Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies, to maintain their tactical knowledge and expertise while remaining relevant to the Armor force.', 'd2d8c2c6aa0d238b94868cdc26929c056d038ac1e4d1264ac0a1fd060d25fcfc', 16, 16, '16', 82, null, null, false, null),
  ('17857469-3f13-50f5-a49c-01eed51c2378', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'UMO, UPL, EOL, MFT, MRT.', '24e7dc47cb53bd6cb8e7c01e1e0a4b99c6073b2e17612df0f18bf23356728bf0', 16, 16, '16', 83, null, null, false, null),
  ('b8098622-06b2-55cc-926b-6d770e4fbecd', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'The KD assignment for 19D Sergeants First Class is Platoon Sergeant. More than any other KD position, Platoon Sergeant is the assignment a Soldier must have, and excel in, to advance to Master Sergeant. Due to Army’s manning requirements and limited positions, SFCs should aggressively seek to complete duties as a Platoon Sergeant prior to serving in a broadening assignment. Armor Proponent defines Platoon Sergeant positions as those within the Operating Force, Opposing Force (OPFOR) elements at the Combat Training Centers (JMRC, JRTC, NTC), or within 194th Armored Brigade or 316th Cavalry Brigade, Fort Benning, GA. Armor Proponent’s guidance is for every SFC to serve a minimum of 18-24 months as a Platoon Sergeant. There are no substitutions for this KD position.', 'e2110fd871eda0daf7bf7a6a98485fd3e86f67fb0b48137b275a093bf8054726', 16, 16, '16', 84, null, null, false, null),
  ('906eb549-531d-5b28-b117-6c8ced7e6791', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', '19D SFCs who have successfully served as a Platoon Sergeant may be selected to serve as a Career Manager, Talent Manager , OC/T, EOA, IG NCO, Senior Drill Sergeant, Senior Instructor, MSI, Training Developer/Writer, Combat Development NCO, or Senior Training Management NCO. SFCs may also serve in various echelons of staff as an Operations Sergeant or Master Gunner. The combination of KD and', '6b2eb6141beb1e028e20a8c3c22f9ca18aadf46f23985738202aa37b0f0cdb21', 16, 16, '16', 85, null, null, false, null),
  ('23767f75-4388-59b4-ae80-a3127fccffdb', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — broadening assignments', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'broadening assignments will provide the NCO with the full range of KSBs required to be successful at the next level of leadership. 19D SFCs who have completed their KD requirements may volunteer to serve in a Security Forces Assistance Brigade (SFAB) Cavalry Squadron as a training/advise NCOIC or assistant operations sergeant.', '33dc19b4dca4afbc5523169ea64039c1595a53d9607e2971a709a6931d4bae1f', 16, 17, '16', 86, null, null, false, null),
  ('6bee2a9b-d54e-50f9-858c-662ebfe533c5', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Training', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'NCOs within the Armor Branch must continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both functional training and PME.', '35cdf5f1af57a4be8515b8cb2d888819d52ee054d2b1d545c5bf0224c423536e', 17, 17, '17', 87, null, null, false, null),
  ('56906c78-4bea-5d33-a8cd-2ce794209b80', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers with an opportunity to acquire additional duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses. 19D SFCs should seek to expand upon their professional development through completion of one or more of the following courses: Ranger, BMG, CLC, SLC, MLMC, and Battle Staff NCO.', '76dc9aa4814aebed1eda83e3183cb1ceb8c0de253acd55a1bc75c51a14275d0f', 17, 17, '17', 88, null, null, false, null),
  ('0285e91e-8e0c-5dec-aa84-7bf1aab393eb', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 17, 17, '17', 89, null, null, false, null),
  ('da641fdd-c3d5-5ce6-9d6a-29f84c5b1c67', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-Development', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. For 19D SFCs serving in broadening assignments, Armor Proponent’s guidance is to continually study Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies, to maintain their tactical knowledge and expertise while remaining relevant to the Armor force.', 'fc004b0735ab729955876f3839d122c82d86b8f3f37f7eaf2ffd8b23255fe64c', 17, 17, '17', 90, null, null, false, null),
  ('4adb9d87-c3e8-5e58-bf84-a4af752d15b7', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19D', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 8. Military Occupational Specialty 19D Cavalry Scout', 'EOA, MRT.', '240e3f3d27cd13bc7ee5965d1ff1918073c20672f6ef74b19d68382817d23655', 17, 17, '17', 91, null, null, false, null),
  ('01c054b9-7038-50f6-ac79-5b93a78ff345', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Armor Crewmembers should focus on proficiency, while building mastery as they progress in their career in 19K critical tasks and warrior tasks and battle drills (See Army Training Network, at: https://atn.army.mil). Institutionally, Tankers should complete PME BLC, ALC, M-SLC, and MLC. Tankers should expand their professional development by completing other functional courses such as Abrams Master Gunner (AMG) Course, MLMC, Battle Staff NCO, CLC, MPF Commander Course, and Tank Commander Course. Troop schools such as Unit Armorer, Unit Movement Officer (UMO), HAZMAT, Unit Prevention Leader (UPL), Master Driver, Unit Safety Officer and Environmental Compliance should be sought after as these courses enhance unit effectiveness and establish well-rounded NCOs. *Note: The above-mentioned courses, including the ones listed in the remainder of this chapter, are not all inclusive and are in no way indicative of the potential for promotion.', 'bc25b24c01188ef24845af223da0adc4c864a1f7bc22afddcc07213a6b6ad2f2', 18, 18, '18', 92, null, null, false, null),
  ('2a26e552-378f-56b7-805a-3f8304170199', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', '19K Soldiers should be focused on attaining crucial experience as a driver or loader on either the Abrams or MPF platforms. Soldiers should focus on successful performance in these positions, developing technical skills, honing tactical proficiency, and laying a foundation of tactical knowledge. Soldiers should strive to serve in positions of increased responsibility, such as Gunner, when provided the opportunity.', '079c5eb6244de6dd9868404cf6adbfcf205cbdf486791ac3de3c57e4b896c329', 18, 18, '18', 93, null, null, false, null),
  ('5ebf68f7-04a0-5459-9117-18d13f79cc6b', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'None.', '903ea500e7ccf842c1312b6c2f964e3e98ff146456cecec717e9a0e122bf735f', 18, 18, '18', 94, null, null, false, null),
  ('e98cca79-3a71-542d-8754-2af5dc80b712', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Training', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Armor Crewmembers must also continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, Soldiers augment their self-development with both', '0951947c41f9ea8d85aba46347c39b9fa0866b7204b0ae926d153486aa655a1d', 19, 19, '19', 95, null, null, false, null),
  ('b3bec14c-cbb9-5cfe-b397-5f17dcdc16be', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Courses prepare Armor Crewmembers for', '0b26a0d7a7b2a351ef379e364b6a1fa90df839ef5fc6f5d8d40424e178352668', 19, 19, '19', 96, null, null, false, null),
  ('c01316ba-769b-5bfd-8950-e7012f1d250d', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — assignment', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers with an opportunity to acquire additional duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses.', '3b005e9bb20a4498b2b537f049181132c84c9533db8e5eaebb2fefc090f0fa08', 19, 19, '19', 97, null, null, false, null),
  ('d5fb92ae-d611-52bb-a00f-3dbf3e152c9f', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 19, 19, '19', 98, null, null, false, null),
  ('fd1a1e98-8954-5608-9e49-51f99d349b96', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. Studying Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies. TC 3-20.31 (Training and Qualification, Crew); TC 3-20.31-1 (Gunnery Skills Test).', 'd41ae39608ace8494bef5eb966ced143269352e44f0acdd424af3d84b79c6505', 19, 19, '19', 99, null, null, false, null),
  ('68553388-7257-5e1c-acbb-351b25af4689', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private-Specialist/Corporal — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'DTMS, Environmental Compliance, Unit Armorer', '518329028dcf00b4bb7025766d28059eb0aced68c95f88dc60cb343044bd532a', 19, 19, '19', 100, null, null, false, null),
  ('92ad0f61-62fb-5656-88c8-d4c250943f89', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', '19K SGTs should focus on attaining crucial leadership experience, developing team leadership skills, honing technical expertise, and laying a foundation of tactical knowledge while serving as a Gunner. SGTs should strive to serve in positions of increased responsibility, such as Tank Commander, when provided the opportunity.', 'f9b8452a7a06183b5cf88a6ed94e4da863325237bffbc0e368fa9de0c632a965', 19, 19, '19', 101, null, null, false, null),
  ('770d02ca-a23b-5b7c-8ddc-77c3d8fdf95d', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', '19K SGTs may be selected to serve as Drill Sergeants or Recruiters to fill critical vacancies within TRADOC. SGTs may serve as Operations Assistants, Operations NCO, Operations Sergeant, Instructor Assistant, or Training Management NCO.', '18761e3c4fcba62e74cbc8ef3e65e2a285bbf095c703c5d47d3af64da38570ed', 19, 19, '19', 102, null, null, false, null),
  ('2d65a911-5add-5a2e-9a89-6d79a37f23b4', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Training', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'NCOs within the Armor Branch must also continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both functional training and PME.', 'd8bfe54b9e6586d8a055b75b011655e247fc58184dfc58d399101339509aa4e2', 19, 19, '19', 103, null, null, false, null),
  ('7e21ba31-1373-5ca6-8a48-d6cae310f540', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers an opportunity to acquire duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses. SGTs should seek to expand upon their professional development and platform expertise in preparation to attend AMG Course. SGTs should expand upon their platform expertise through completion of unit led SABOT Academy and the MGPAC in preparation to attend AMG Course.', '5386e1352c662201db4c3128172d3da084e588eb0343a52a6868692dbb43d54c', 19, 19, '19', 104, null, null, false, null),
  ('226fb607-324e-50d8-b9a5-9c62eb90013b', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 19, 19, '19', 105, null, null, false, null),
  ('04578795-0848-5539-b27c-34b354ef25a2', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. Studying Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies. TC 3-20.31-4 (Direct Fire Engagement Process (DIDEA).', 'f49bc852e00e21a38ce21d3a033df7de87e27704dd3575215fec769000ceedc6', 19, 19, '19', 106, null, null, false, null),
  ('75a8afec-fbe3-571b-bcfd-a51aa2e55f94', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'UPL, Master Driver, HAZMAT', 'febb1bc3c9e103b199bc902075e2f1dda5bcafe9ac5e2f070d22de69a92b4992', 19, 19, '19', 107, null, null, false, null),
  ('74066754-3fe3-5470-bde3-b48871d47747', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'The KD assignment for 19K Staff Sergeants is Tank Commander. SSGs should focus on successful performance in this position, refining and developing leadership skills, tactical, and technical expertise. During this stage in a SSG’s career there may be competing requirements that could conflict with career development. SSGs should aggressively seek a KD position prior to serving in a broadening assignment. Armor Proponent defines Tank Commander positions as those within the Operating Force, Opposing Force (OPFOR) elements at the Combat Training Centers (JMRC, JRTC, NTC), or within 1-16th Cavalry Squadron, 316th Cavalry Brigade, Fort Benning. Armor Proponent’s guidance is for SSGs to serve a minimum of 18-24 months as a Tank Commander, or 12 months as a Tank Commander and successively 12 months as an AMG There is no substitution for this KD position.', 'ca76ec3590a6dcab9d69251017eea9c8a5481a456294fd44bdeeeb41b103d78f', 19, 20, '19', 108, null, null, false, null),
  ('43a52fb9-0619-586d-b73f-869f149de944', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', '19K SSGs who have successfully completed their KD requirements may be selected to serve as a Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Instructor, OC/T, Combat Development NCO, or Training Developer/Writer. SSGs may also serve in various echelons of staff as an Assistant Operations Sergeant, Operations Sergeant, or Master Gunner. 19K SSGs are not authorized to serve within the Security Forces Assistance Brigades (SFABs).', '0484797d886bd2d006e55228b748dec528fa27170dc120b10c9dbfc7a0b46132', 20, 20, '20', 109, null, null, false, null),
  ('08e93fe0-5a83-50b2-aa36-156813d271a1', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Training', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'NCOs within the Armor Branch must continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both functional training and PME', '9fc0ee736d7cc99049b3c94b0ca0bb0b8364af3ebf21a29de6992e4d51088beb', 20, 20, '20', 110, null, null, false, null),
  ('71d44d9a-53cb-5f0d-82d1-28e3347cf55b', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers with an opportunity to acquire additional duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses. MOS 19K SSGs should strive to complete the AMG Course. SSGs should prepare for AMG through unit led SABOT Academy and the MGPAC. Developing the individual traits and technical skills to complete the AMG Course, succeed in KD assignment, and effectively serve as a Master Gunner, requires a level of personal commitment that sets an MOS 19K SSG above their peers. MOS 19K SSGs should further seek to expand upon their professional development through completion of one or more of the following courses: Battle Staff NCO and Master Fitness. SSGs returning to the Operational Force after completion of a DA select assignment are encouraged to attend the Tank Commander Course to restore platform proficiency', '681af5191b1e2afcc88a3f14cca777a1d459930bbbcc7c0b27cbe4f577340ba5', 20, 20, '20', 111, null, null, false, null),
  ('80c3a450-4264-55f6-9c94-3889e65d5cc4', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 20, 20, '20', 112, null, null, false, null),
  ('3d11dd5c-fa2b-5ea7-b0df-85fa22f78a05', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. For SSGs serving in', 'a2be84df4b17b9e2b1d8c5c8fc9f6f8e62158f0440326ba2cc4441efb1b81d29', 20, 20, '20', 113, null, null, false, null),
  ('ee7919b3-9e58-5420-b927-0fdb2de74b85', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — broadening assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'broadening assignments, Armor Proponent’s guidance is to continually study Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies, to maintain their tactical knowledge and expertise while remaining relevant to the Armor force.', 'd2d8c2c6aa0d238b94868cdc26929c056d038ac1e4d1264ac0a1fd060d25fcfc', 20, 20, '20', 114, null, null, false, null),
  ('2229fddf-dc36-52ad-9b7b-80777df2777f', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'UMO, UPL, EOL, MFT, MRT.', '24e7dc47cb53bd6cb8e7c01e1e0a4b99c6073b2e17612df0f18bf23356728bf0', 20, 20, '20', 115, null, null, false, null),
  ('bc81f187-388c-5342-88a3-0b83b1cf6ba9', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational Assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'The KD assignment for 19K SFCs is Platoon Sergeant. More than any other KD position, Platoon Sergeant is the assignment an NCO must have, and excel in, to advance to Master Sergeant. Due to the Army’s manning requirements and limited positions, SFCs should aggressively seek to complete duties as a Platoon Sergeant prior to serving in broadening assignments. Armor Proponent defines Platoon Sergeant positions as those within the Operating Force, Opposing Force (OPFOR) elements at the Combat Training Centers (JMRC, JRTC, NTC), or within 1-16th Cavalry Squadron, 316th Cavalry Brigade, Fort Benning. Armor Proponent’s guidance is for SFCs to serve a minimum of 18-24 months as a Platoon Sergeant. There are no substitutions for this KD position.', '2c625d9c1a169be23be24a869a95ddc418d131fc127c33b546e04e3538f2e75a', 20, 21, '20', 116, null, null, false, null),
  ('cc647b54-3d62-562c-a2f7-5e825cadc6d0', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening Assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', '19K SFCs who have successfully served as a Platoon Sergeant may be selected to serve as a Career Manager, Talent Manager, OC/T, EOA, IG NCO, Senior Drill Sergeant, Senior Instructor, MSI, Training Developer/Writer, Combat Development NCO, or Senior Training Management NCO. SFCs may also serve in various echelons of staff as a Master Gunner, Assistant Operations Sergeant, or Operations Sergeant. A combination of KD and broadening assignments will provide the NCO with the full range of knowledge, skills and behaviors required to be successful at the next level of leadership. 19K SFCs are not authorized to serve within the Security Forces Assistance Brigades (SFABs).', 'e0f0175307ea12b2dc7425c58f1f2075888d9b2c033ab5a4b1b331073d859890', 21, 21, '21', 117, null, null, false, null),
  ('39218b3c-05c8-5b5f-af45-fd84fb4e27ef', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Training', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'NCOs within the Armor Branch must continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both functional training and PME.', '35cdf5f1af57a4be8515b8cb2d888819d52ee054d2b1d545c5bf0224c423536e', 21, 21, '21', 118, null, null, false, null),
  ('1eab4100-990f-54aa-aa24-06e7bdb6ae4b', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers an opportunity to acquire duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses. MOS 19K SFCs should strive to complete the Abrams Master Gunner Course. SFCs should prepare for AMG through unit led SABOT Academy and the MGPAC. Developing the individual traits and technical skills to complete the AMG Course, succeed in KD assignment, and effectively serve as a Master Gunner, requires a level of personal commitment that sets an MOS 19K SFC above their peers. SFCs should further seek to expand upon their professional development through completion of one or more of the following courses: CLC, MLMC, and Battle Staff NCO.', '1a387a07e1c5aa3c1e642d9f8d6b1d091daeea77a18f7fd895894bdd30c71638', 21, 21, '21', 119, null, null, false, null),
  ('1978dedd-6d40-5b36-bdeb-62be7bc93609', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 21, 21, '21', 120, null, null, false, null),
  ('cbeb3470-3062-5b28-8877-0a6b91cab281', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-Development', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. For SFCs serving in', '34e7e23f235d418fcf93e358ddae5d90379f35919e6d9ad2ffe645207cb1c49e', 21, 21, '21', 121, null, null, false, null),
  ('9e4e89e5-f012-59da-8ecd-1ab8e8e4efc8', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — broadening assignments', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'broadening assignments, Armor Proponent’s guidance is to continually study Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies, to maintain their tactical knowledge and expertise while remaining relevant to the Armor Force.', 'eb316f30ac9e02ec9476cb1aa4ae93fac820ddfbfbfd7f2cf7daced1a4d99837', 21, 21, '21', 122, null, null, false, null),
  ('5ebbe9de-7a0f-545e-b38d-f2a1100b7b76', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19K', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional Duties', 'Chapter 11. Military Occupational Specialty 19K Armor Crewmember', 'EOA, MRT.', '240e3f3d27cd13bc7ee5965d1ff1918073c20672f6ef74b19d68382817d23655', 21, 21, '21', 123, null, null, false, null),
  ('4495eaab-fe85-572d-9407-f5261343ecd9', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'At this point in the Armor Senior Sergeants’ career, they should be focused on mastering the warfighting skills required for their skill levels, and successfully completing all NCOPDS, attending professional development schools, and serving operational time on Battalion, Brigade, or higher staff.', '1fac9a150ed83a1c825f5e4f69b70e2979847e24a5979669710fe5807a4ca425', 22, 22, '22', 124, null, null, false, null),
  ('df93b47a-07c9-5d9c-9ce5-a63826ba2cf5', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Operational Assignment', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'The KD position for 19Z MSG is First Sergeant (1SG). Due to Army manning requirements and limited positions, MSGs should aggressively seek to complete duties as a 1SG prior to serving in a broadening assignment. Without a successful tour as a 1SG, MSGs will not be competitive for Sergeant Major. After serving as a 1SG within a Troop or Company, Armor Proponent highly encourages MSGs to pursue additional 1SG responsibilities within a Headquarters Troop/Company or Security Forces Assistance Brigade (SFAB) Cavalry Squadron. MSGs that have successfully served as HHT or HHC 1SG have shown a higher propensity for selection to the Sergeants Major Academy. KD complete MSGs should take the opportunity to fill a Squadron/Battalion Operations Sergeant position when possible. Armor Proponent’s guidance is for MSGs to serve a minimum of 24 months as a 1SG. There are no substitutions for this KD time.', '1aa6422a37958d9a574a01781c80a15e12d6dfbc96fda5e6e221660c28f62473', 22, 23, '22', 125, null, null, false, null),
  ('50ff0939-f251-56e9-b978-1d91a2fd804a', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Broadening Assignment', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'MSGs who have successfully served as a 1SG may be selected to serve as a Senior Career Manager, Senior Talent Manager, Senior Military Science Instructor (SMSI), OC/T, EOA, IG NCO, Senior Instructor, Training Development/Writer, Combat Development NCO, NCOA 1SG, or Senior Training Management NCO. MSGs may also serve in various echelons of staff as an Operations Sergeant or Master Gunner. A combination of KD and broadening assignments will provide NCOs with the full range of knowledge, skills and behaviors required to be successful at the next level or leadership.', '8bd1bd2064bf5bcf52b56f7572dd78744c8789a8a44a686ccedce0cf186ee812', 23, 23, '23', 126, null, null, false, null),
  ('4190a576-08fe-5c75-8806-a75d39e2f702', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Training', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'NCOs within Armor Branch must continue to seek developmental opportunities within each domain of training. Primarily, NCOs augment their self-development with both', '68b6060da9dcb18c490a9778e67e1e8df42934df6609f25ec703d25be88d39e0', 23, 23, '23', 127, null, null, false, null),
  ('c960493e-e8e2-5278-8a5e-88fd0b2a1b1a', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Functional Courses/Troop Schools', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'Courses prepare Armor Soldiers for assignment to specific duty positions and increase their value to the branch. These courses provide Soldiers an opportunity to acquire duty position-required skills and knowledge that cannot be obtained by attending other institutional courses.', 'ade96c36057e8cea00f0e45d4d821e3d11f25e0c4c7a66497ea15c75ed3a26f1', 23, 23, '23', 128, null, null, false, null),
  ('54c7b927-c175-584f-8d8f-a346a3c211d4', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'PME is progressive and sequential across a career continuum, to ensure that Soldiers are successful at each stage of their professional service, while continually growing in the competencies and attributes needed for higher levels of service.', '8e48a2a1c7c57eeb786360783bca476f3484535bbcf3a4eb33ec55f9c1e00a88', 23, 23, '23', 129, null, null, false, null),
  ('9a5804f6-e0ff-542d-974d-73d1dfdd0ae2', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Self-Development', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'Completion of college courses/degree program. For MSGs serving in', 'a28864e5a904f100e1a017d80a7e750c22b2ed75c7f63bbb471fd567a7264752', 23, 23, '23', 130, null, null, false, null),
  ('efb2290a-7f5f-5713-96e9-17c4869a2c64', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — broadening assignments', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'broadening assignments, Armor Proponent’s guidance is to continually study Army publications directly related to MOS proficiency and core competencies, to maintain their tactical knowledge and expertise while remaining relevant to the Armor Force.', 'eb316f30ac9e02ec9476cb1aa4ae93fac820ddfbfbfd7f2cf7daced1a4d99837', 23, 23, '23', 131, null, null, false, null),
  ('0a2bd128-b01f-5387-b0a5-539c929113ca', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant — Additional Training', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'MSGs designated to serve in a Cavalry organization are highly encouraged to attend CLC, Joint Fire Power Control, and Battle Staff NCO.', 'c0984115ecd9edcc45739806697eb06d7a4b993c48e5896deb8354ca316a327f', 23, 23, '23', 132, null, null, false, null),
  ('f538bbbb-4e67-5163-bfbd-c17aa4b213e5', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major — Operational Assignment', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'The principal assignment for SGMs, other than CSM, is battalion level or higher operations sergeant or staff assignments at division level or above.', '26c59b55eee18f4ed1f4c6cee664c013f7ae2f530d03c928bb69107b92dafae3', 23, 23, '23', 133, null, null, false, null),
  ('8712fd7b-5144-5020-b392-79e8c0296ce5', 'edae8a9a-ae10-54a7-bf9b-35d57d16a550', 'Army', 'enlisted', '19Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major — Broadening Assignment', 'Chapter 14. Military Occupational Specialty 19Z Armor Senior Sergeant', 'All assignments are handled by Talent Alignment and Development Directorate (TADD), Human Resource Command (HRC), Sergeants Major Management Division (SMMD).', '9d7d55e0ba707f5af8083ba5966dbd7db6e2d2cebd30f9068c115eaf8b7ed393', 23, 23, '23', 134, null, null, false, null);
